on the class (before `customElements.define`),\n+and calls `attachInternals()` once in the constructor. The\n+`ElementInternals` is stored on `_internals` and reused across\n+reconnect cycles. `makeSetupContext` receives it as an optional\n+parameter and attaches it to the context object only when present.\n+\n+The `ComponentBuilder` carries a `FormAssoc` type parameter\n+(default `false`). The setup callback's context type is intersected\n+with `FormAssociatedContext` when `FormAssoc` is `true`, so\n+`ctx.internals` is a type error without the opt-in.\n+\n+`ctx.form(handlers)` registers handlers for `formResetCallback`,\n+`formDisabledCallback`, `formStateRestoreCallback` and\n+`formAssociatedCallback`. Handlers are stored on instance properties\n+`_fh` (the handlers object) and `_fp` (a pending restore tuple).\n+The prototype callbacks are defined with `function` (not arrow) so\n+`this` refers to the host. Handlers are cleared in teardown by\n+setting `_fh = undefined`. A `restore` callback received before\n+`ctx.form()` is stored in `_fp` and replayed when the handler\n+registers; `reset`, `disabled` and `associated` are not replayed.\n+`FormLifecycleHandlers` is a public type export from `microtags`.\n+\n <!-- redeye:start -->\n ## Agent skills\n \ndiff --git a/CONTEXT.md b/CONTEXT.md\nindex 30424f0..be0661b 100644\n--- a/CONTEXT.md\n+++ b/CONTEXT.md\n@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ _Avoid_: pipeline, config\n \n **Link**:\n One call in the builder chain: `withProps`, `withRefs`, `withContexts`,\n-or `render`. `setup` is the terminal link.\n+`formAssociated`, or `render`. `setup` is the terminal link.\n _Avoid_: step, method (in prose)\n \n **Prop**:\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 640c4e4..5a39678 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ This package adds some provisions for serverside rendering.\n   * [`builder.withRefs(fn)`](#builderwithrefsfn)\n   * [`builder.withContexts`](#builderwithcontexts)\n     + [`.withContexts` Example](#withcontexts-example)\n+  * [`builder.formAssociated()`](#builderformassociated)\n   * [`builder.render(fn, options?)`](#builderrenderfn-options)\n   * [`builder.setup(ctx)`](#buildersetupctx)\n     + [`ctx`](#ctx)\n@@ -556,11 +557,13 @@ The object returned by [`define`](#define). Includes methods:\n | `.withProps(fn)` | `ComponentBuilder` | Declare reactive attributes. See [Props](#props). |\n | `.withRefs(fn)` | `ComponentBuilder` | Declare DOM refs resolved once the element connects. See [Refs](#refs-1). |\n | `.withContexts(fn)` | `ComponentBuilder` | Consume context values published by an ancestor. See [`withContexts`](#withcontexts). |\n+| `.formAssociated()` | `ComponentBuilder` | Make hosts form-associated custom elements. See [`.formAssociated`](#builderformassociated). |\n | `.render(fn, opts?)` | `ComponentBuilder` | Attach a server-render function. See [`.render`](#builderrenderfn-options) below. Not to be confused with the DOM helper [`microtags/render`](#microtagsrender). |\n | `.setup(fn)` | `MicrotagElementClass` | Registers the custom element and returns its class. See [`setup`](#setup) below. |\n \n-Methods `withProps`, `withRefs`, and `withContexts` each return a new builder,\n-so they chain in any order; `setup` ends the chain by registering the element.\n+Methods `withProps`, `withRefs`, `withContexts` and `formAssociated` each\n+return a new builder, so they chain in any order; `setup` ends the chain by\n+registering the element.\n \n ---------------------------------------------------------\n \n@@ -778,6 +781,68 @@ define('themed-card')\n \n ---------------------------------------------------------\n \n+### `builder.formAssociated()`\n+\n+Make hosts of this component form-associated custom elements. The host\n+gets an `ElementInternals` object, available in setup as\n+`ctx.internals`. With it the component can call `setFormValue`,\n+`setValidity`, set ARIA defaults, and participate in the containing\n+form.\n+\n+```ts\n+class ComponentBuilder {\n+    formAssociated ():ComponentBuilder<\n+        Props, RefDefs, CtxDefs, true\n+    >\n+}\n+```\n+\n+A form-associated host:\n+\n+- contributes a value to `FormData` under its `name` attribute\n+- takes part in constraint validation (`:valid` / `:invalid`)\n+- follows `disabled` from an ancestor `<fieldset>`\n+- exposes `ctx.internals.form` as the enclosing form\n+\n+```ts\n+const RatingInput = define('rating-input')\n+    .withProps(p => ({ value: p.number() }))\n+    .formAssociated()\n+    .setup(ctx => {\n+        ctx.internals.role = 'slider'\n+        ctx.effect(() => {\n+            ctx.internals.setFormValue(\n+                String(ctx.props.value())\n+            )\n+        })\n+    })\n+```\n+\n+#### `ctx.form(handlers)`\n+\n+Register handlers for the form lifecycle callbacks. All four are\n+optional:\n+\n+```ts\n+ctx.form({\n+    reset () { /* form was reset */ },\n+    disabled (isDisabled) { /* fieldset toggled */ },\n+    restore (state, mode) { /* autocomplete / back-forward */ },\n+    associated (form) { /* moved into or out of a form */ },\n+})\n+```\n+\n+Calling `ctx.form()` again replaces the earlier handlers. Handlers\n+are dropped when the host tears down. A `restore` callback that fires\n+before setup has registered a handler is replayed once the handler is\n+set; `reset`, `disabled` and `associated` are not replayed because\n+their state is readable at setup time (`host.matches(':disabled')`,\n+`ctx.internals.form`).\n+\n+Components that do not call `.formAssociated()` behave exactly as\n+before and do not appear in `FormData`.\n+\n+---------------------------------------------------------\n \n ### `builder.render(fn, options?)`\n \ndiff --git a/docs/adr/ADR-012-form-associated-components.md b/docs/adr/ADR-012-form-associated-components.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..754293c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/adr/ADR-012-form-associated-components.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@\n+# ADR-012: Form-associated custom elements\n+\n+**Date:** 2026-11-24\n+\n+**Status:** Accepted\n+\n+**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size)\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+A component author who wants to build a form control (a custom input,\n+a rich text field, a rating widget) cannot make it a real form control\n+with microtags. The platform way is a form-associated custom element:\n+the class sets a static `formAssociated = true`, each host gets an\n+`ElementInternals` from `attachInternals()`, and the browser wires it\n+into the containing form for submission, validation, and disabled\n+state. Microtags calls `customElements.define` inside `setup()` with\n+no way to set the static first, and does not expose\n+`ElementInternals` to the setup callback.\n+\n+The first consumer is `markdown-area`, a `<textarea>` replacement.\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+A new builder link, `.formAssociated()`, opts a component into the\n+platform's form-associated custom element behaviour. It takes no\n+arguments.\n+\n+- **Builder link.** `.formAssociated()` returns a new builder with an\n+  internal `formAssociated` flag. The flag propagates through all\n+  subsequent links. It composes with `withProps`, `withRefs`,\n+  `withContexts` and `render` in any order.\n+\n+- **Static.** The factory sets `static formAssociated = true` on the\n+  generated class before the builder calls `customElements.define`,\n+  so the browser reads it at define time.\n+\n+- **Internals.** A form-associated host calls `attachInternals()`\n+  once, in its constructor. The result is kept on the instance and\n+  reused across disconnect/reconnect cycles. Setup receives it as\n+  `ctx.internals`.\n+\n+- **Setup context.** For a form-associated component the setup context\n+  gains `internals:ElementInternals`. Components that did not opt in\n+  get a type error when they read `ctx.internals`.\n+\n+- **Form lifecycle callbacks.** The class installs\n+  `formResetCallback`, `formDisabledCallback`,\n+  `formStateRestoreCallback` and `formAssociatedCallback` on the\n+  prototype. Each forwards to handlers registered through the\n+  `ctx.form(handlers)` method. The `restore` callback is replayed\n+  when a handler is registered; the others are not (their state is\n+  readable from the host and `internals`). Calling `ctx.form()` again\n+  replaces the earlier handlers. Handlers are dropped on teardown.\n+\n+- **Server render.** `render-support` is unchanged: form association\n+  has no server-side meaning.\n+\n+- **Types.** `FormAssociatedContext` is a public type export from\n+  `microtags`, so declaration emit in consuming packages does not hit\n+  TS2883. The builder carries a `FormAssoc` type parameter that\n+  controls whether the setup context includes `internals`.\n+\n+## Size cost\n+\n+| Entry | Before | After | Delta |\n+|-------|--------|-------|-------|\n+| `microtags` (core, ticket 02) | 4.04 kB | 4.09 kB | +50 B |\n+| `microtags` (core, ticket 03) | 4.09 kB | 4.23 kB | +140 B |\n+\n+The ticket 02 delta (50 B) covers the `formAssociated` static, the\n+`attachInternals()` call in the constructor, and passing internals to\n+the setup context. The ticket 03 delta (140 B) adds four prototype\n+callbacks, `ctx.form()` with handler storage, and restore replay.\n+Both are under the 150 B-per-ticket target.\n+\n+## Consequences\n+\n+- Authors can build form controls that submit values, participate in\n+  constraint validation, follow `disabled` from ancestor fieldsets,\n+  and hear about form reset and state restore.\n+- Components that do not opt in pay no runtime cost and no API change.\n+- The core entry limit rises from 4.1 kB to 4.25 kB.\n+\n+[adr-004]: ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\ndiff --git a/docs/adr/INDEX.md b/docs/adr/INDEX.md\nindex 374a97c..6dcaf45 100644\n--- a/docs/adr/INDEX.md\n+++ b/docs/adr/INDEX.md\n@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ consume these and `CONTEXT.md` for the project glossary.\n | [ADR-009][adr-009] | Server render support loaded through the render link (amends ADR-005) | 2026-10-14 |\n | [ADR-010][adr-010] | Preact owns the host, the element owns its children | 2026-11-08 |\n | [ADR-011][adr-011] | Core renders an empty host with a kept render link (amends ADR-010) | 2026-11-10 |\n+| [ADR-012][adr-012] | Form-associated custom elements | 2026-11-24 |\n \n [adr-006]: ADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md\n [adr-007]: ADR-007-client-templater.md\n@@ -24,3 +25,4 @@ consume these and `CONTEXT.md` for the project glossary.\n [adr-009]: ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md\n [adr-010]: ADR-010-preact-adapter-ownership-split.md\n [adr-011]: ADR-011-core-renders-empty-host.md\n+[adr-012]: ADR-012-form-associated-components.md\ndiff --git a/src/builders.ts b/src/builders.ts\nindex a9b1612..8a160d8 100644\n--- a/src/builders.ts\n+++ b/src/builders.ts\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ import type {\n     PropType,\n     PropertyOnlyProp,\n     SetupContext,\n+    FormAssociatedContext,\n     Coercer,\n     RefDef,\n     SingleRefDef,\n@@ -204,46 +205,48 @@ export type MicrotagElementClass<\n  * Fluent builder that accumulates props/refs/contexts config\n  * before registering a custom element via `.setup()`.\n  */\n+interface BuilderConfig {\n+    tag:string\n+    coercers:Record<string, Coercer<unknown>>\n+    observed:string[]\n+    propNames:string[]\n+    propMetas:Record<string, PropMeta>\n+    refDefs:Record<string, RefDef>\n+    ctxDefs:Record<string, ContextToken<unknown>>\n+    renderFn?:RenderFn<any, any>\n+    formAssociated?:boolean\n+}\n+\n export class ComponentBuilder<\n     Props extends Record<string, PropDef> = Record<never, never>,\n     RefDefs extends Record<string, RefDef> = Record<never, never>,\n-    CtxDefs extends Record<string, ContextToken<unknown>> = Record<never, never>,\n+    CtxDefs extends Record<string, ContextToken<unknown>> = (\n+        Record<never, never>\n+    ),\n+    FormAssoc extends boolean = false,\n > {\n-    private readonly _coercers:Record<string, Coercer<unknown>>\n-    private readonly _observed:string[]\n-    private readonly _propNames:string[]\n-    private readonly _propMetas:Record<string, PropMeta>\n-    private readonly _refDefs:Record<string, RefDef>\n-    private readonly _ctxDefs:Record<string, ContextToken<unknown>>\n-    private readonly _renderFn?:RenderFn<Props, RefDefs>\n-\n-    constructor (\n-        readonly tagName:string,\n-        coercers:Record<string, Coercer<unknown>> = {},\n-        observed:string[] = [],\n-        refDefs:Record<string, RefDef> = {},\n-        ctxDefs:Record<string, ContextToken<unknown>> = {},\n-        propNames:string[] = [],\n-        propMetas:Record<string, PropMeta> = {},\n-        renderFn?:RenderFn<any, any>,\n-    ) {\n-        this._coercers = coercers\n-        this._observed = observed\n-        this._propNames = propNames\n-        this._propMetas = propMetas\n-        this._refDefs = refDefs\n-        this._ctxDefs = ctxDefs\n-        this._renderFn = renderFn as\n-            RenderFn<Props, RefDefs> | undefined\n+    private readonly _c:BuilderConfig\n+\n+    constructor (cfg:string | BuilderConfig) {\n+        this._c = typeof cfg === 'string' ?\n+            {\n+                tag: cfg,\n+                coercers: {},\n+                observed: [],\n+                propNames: [],\n+                propMetas: {},\n+                refDefs: {},\n+                ctxDefs: {},\n+            } :\n+            cfg\n+    }\n+\n+    get tagName ():string {\n+        return this._c.tag\n     }\n \n-    /**\n-     * The custom element tag name, e.g. 'my-counter'. Available at every\n-     * point in the fluent chain since each builder method returns a new\n-     * builder carrying the same tag name.\n-     */\n     get TAG ():string {\n-        return this.tagName\n+        return this._c.tag\n     }\n \n     withProps<P extends Record<string, PropDef>> (\n@@ -280,63 +283,55 @@ export class ComponentBuilder<\n             }\n         }\n \n-        return new ComponentBuilder<P, RefDefs, CtxDefs>(\n-            this.tagName,\n+        return new ComponentBuilder<P, RefDefs, CtxDefs, FormAssoc>({\n+            ...this._c,\n             coercers,\n             observed,\n-            this._refDefs,\n-            this._ctxDefs,\n             propNames,\n             propMetas,\n-        )\n+            renderFn: undefined,\n+        })\n     }\n \n     withRefs<R extends Record<string, RefDef>> (\n         fn:(r:RefsDSL) => R\n-    ):ComponentBuilder<Props, R, CtxDefs> {\n+    ):ComponentBuilder<Props, R, CtxDefs, FormAssoc> {\n         const defs = fn(refsDSL)\n-        return new ComponentBuilder<Props, R, CtxDefs>(\n-            this.tagName,\n-            this._coercers,\n-            this._observed,\n-            defs,\n-            this._ctxDefs,\n-            this._propNames,\n-            this._propMetas,\n-            this._renderFn,\n-        )\n+        return new ComponentBuilder<Props, R, CtxDefs, FormAssoc>({\n+            ...this._c,\n+            refDefs: defs,\n+        })\n     }\n \n     withContexts<C extends Record<string, ContextToken<unknown>>> (\n         fn:(c:ContextDSL) => C\n-    ):ComponentBuilder<Props, RefDefs, C> {\n+    ):ComponentBuilder<Props, RefDefs, C, FormAssoc> {\n         const defs = fn(contextDSL)\n-        return new ComponentBuilder<Props, RefDefs, C>(\n-            this.tagName,\n-            this._coercers,\n-            this._observed,\n-            this._refDefs,\n-            defs,\n-            this._propNames,\n-            this._propMetas,\n-            this._renderFn,\n-        )\n+        return new ComponentBuilder<Props, RefDefs, C, FormAssoc>({\n+            ...this._c,\n+            ctxDefs: defs,\n+        })\n+    }\n+\n+    formAssociated ():ComponentBuilder<\n+        Props, RefDefs, CtxDefs, true\n+    > {\n+        return new ComponentBuilder<\n+            Props, RefDefs, CtxDefs, true\n+        >({\n+            ...this._c,\n+            formAssociated: true,\n+        })\n     }\n \n     render (\n         fn:RenderFn<Props, RefDefs>,\n         _optio