{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W8ZA6LaLfxmAv3DoECLVRU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tdiff --git a/.size-limit.js b/.size-limit.js\n2\tindex 31b95f1..5491244 100644\n3\t--- a/.size-limit.js\n4\t+++ b/.size-limit.js\n5\t@@ -8,9 +8,12 @@ export default [\n6\t         // renderParts static; 4.06 kB with an empty host rendered\n7\t         // through a kept render link (ADR-011); 4.03 kB with comments\n8\t         // counted as content; 4.04 kB skipping define for a tag that\n9\t-        // is already registered, rounded up to the next\n10\t-        // 0.05 kB\n11\t-        limit: '4.1 kB',\n12\t+        // is already registered; 4.04 kB after builder config object\n13\t+        // refactor (positional args -> single config); 4.09 kB with\n14\t+        // form-associated custom element support (ADR-012); 4.23 kB\n15\t+        // with form lifecycle handlers (ctx.form), rounded up to the\n16\t+        // next 0.05 kB\n17\t+        limit: '4.25 kB',\n18\t     },\n19\t     {\n20\t         name: 'microtags/htm',\n21\tdiff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md\n22\tindex 5c16637..a15eb80 100644\n23\t--- a/AGENTS.md\n24\t+++ b/AGENTS.md\n25\t@@ -518,6 +518,32 @@ tapout run, so tests for it capture the queued task with the\n26\t `insertBefore` fallback in Chromium, set `moveBefore` to `undefined` on\n27\t the parent instance.\n28\t \n29\t+### Form-associated components (`src/builders.ts`, `src/factory.ts`, ADR-012)\n30\t+\n31\t+`.formAssociated()` in the builder chain sets a `formAssociated` flag\n32\t+on `BuilderConfig`. The factory reads it, defines `static\n33\t+formAssociated = true` on the class (before `customElements.define`),\n34\t+and calls `attachInternals()` once in the constructor. The\n35\t+`ElementInternals` is stored on `_internals` and reused across\n36\t+reconnect cycles. `makeSetupContext` receives it as an optional\n37\t+parameter and attaches it to the context object only when present.\n38\t+\n39\t+The `ComponentBuilder` carries a `FormAssoc` type parameter\n40\t+(default `false`). The setup callback's context type is intersected\n41\t+with `FormAssociatedContext` when `FormAssoc` is `true`, so\n42\t+`ctx.internals` is a type error without the opt-in.\n43\t+\n44\t+`ctx.form(handlers)` registers handlers for `formResetCallback`,\n45\t+`formDisabledCallback`, `formStateRestoreCallback` and\n46\t+`formAssociatedCallback`. Handlers are stored on instance properties\n47\t+`_fh` (the handlers object) and `_fp` (a pending restore tuple).\n48\t+The prototype callbacks are defined with `function` (not arrow) so\n49\t+`this` refers to the host. Handlers are cleared in teardown by\n50\t+setting `_fh = undefined`. A `restore` callback received before\n51\t+`ctx.form()` is stored in `_fp` and replayed when the handler\n52\t+registers; `reset`, `disabled` and `associated` are not replayed.\n53\t+`FormLifecycleHandlers` is a public type export from `microtags`.\n54\t+\n55\t <!-- redeye:start -->\n56\t ## Agent skills\n57\t \n58\tdiff --git a/CONTEXT.md b/CONTEXT.md\n59\tindex 30424f0..be0661b 100644\n60\t--- a/CONTEXT.md\n61\t+++ b/CONTEXT.md\n62\t@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ _Avoid_: pipeline, config\n63\t \n64\t **Link**:\n65\t One call in the builder chain: `withProps`, `withRefs`, `withContexts`,\n66\t-or `render`. `setup` is the terminal link.\n67\t+`formAssociated`, or `render`. `setup` is the terminal link.\n68\t _Avoid_: step, method (in prose)\n69\t \n70\t **Prop**:\n71\tdiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\n72\tindex 640c4e4..5a39678 100644\n73\t--- a/README.md\n74\t+++ b/README.md\n75\t@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ This package adds some provisions for serverside rendering.\n76\t   * [`builder.withRefs(fn)`](#builderwithrefsfn)\n77\t   * [`builder.withContexts`](#builderwithcontexts)\n78\t     + [`.withContexts` Example](#withcontexts-example)\n79\t+  * [`builder.formAssociated()`](#builderformassociated)\n80\t   * [`builder.render(fn, options?)`](#builderrenderfn-options)\n81\t   * [`builder.setup(ctx)`](#buildersetupctx)\n82\t     + [`ctx`](#ctx)\n83\t@@ -556,11 +557,13 @@ The object returned by [`define`](#define). Includes methods:\n84\t | `.withProps(fn)` | `ComponentBuilder` | Declare reactive attributes. See [Props](#props). |\n85\t | `.withRefs(fn)` | `ComponentBuilder` | Declare DOM refs resolved once the element connects. See [Refs](#refs-1). |\n86\t | `.withContexts(fn)` | `ComponentBuilder` | Consume context values published by an ancestor. See [`withContexts`](#withcontexts). |\n87\t+| `.formAssociated()` | `ComponentBuilder` | Make hosts form-associated custom elements. See [`.formAssociated`](#builderformassociated). |\n88\t | `.render(fn, opts?)` | `ComponentBuilder` | Attach a server-render function. See [`.render`](#builderrenderfn-options) below. Not to be confused with the DOM helper [`microtags/render`](#microtagsrender). |\n89\t | `.setup(fn)` | `MicrotagElementClass` | Registers the custom element and returns its class. See [`setup`](#setup) below. |\n90\t \n91\t-Methods `withProps`, `withRefs`, and `withContexts` each return a new builder,\n92\t-so they chain in any order; `setup` ends the chain by registering the element.\n93\t+Methods `withProps`, `withRefs`, `withContexts` and `formAssociated` each\n94\t+return a new builder, so they chain in any order; `setup` ends the chain by\n95\t+registering the element.\n96\t \n97\t ---------------------------------------------------------\n98\t \n99\t@@ -778,6 +781,68 @@ define('themed-card')\n100\t \n101\t ---------------------------------------------------------\n102\t \n103\t+### `builder.formAssociated()`\n104\t+\n105\t+Make hosts of this component form-associated custom elements. The host\n106\t+gets an `ElementInternals` object, available in setup as\n107\t+`ctx.internals`. With it the component can call `setFormValue`,\n108\t+`setValidity`, set ARIA defaults, and participate in the containing\n109\t+form.\n110\t+\n111\t+```ts\n112\t+class ComponentBuilder {\n113\t+    formAssociated ():ComponentBuilder<\n114\t+        Props, RefDefs, CtxDefs, true\n115\t+    >\n116\t+}\n117\t+```\n118\t+\n119\t+A form-associated host:\n120\t+\n121\t+- contributes a value to `FormData` under its `name` attribute\n122\t+- takes part in constraint validation (`:valid` / `:invalid`)\n123\t+- follows `disabled` from an ancestor `<fieldset>`\n124\t+- exposes `ctx.internals.form` as the enclosing form\n125\t+\n126\t+```ts\n127\t+const RatingInput = define('rating-input')\n128\t+    .withProps(p => ({ value: p.number() }))\n129\t+    .formAssociated()\n130\t+    .setup(ctx => {\n131\t+        ctx.internals.role = 'slider'\n132\t+        ctx.effect(() => {\n133\t+            ctx.internals.setFormValue(\n134\t+                String(ctx.props.value())\n135\t+            )\n136\t+        })\n137\t+    })\n138\t+```\n139\t+\n140\t+#### `ctx.form(handlers)`\n141\t+\n142\t+Register handlers for the form lifecycle callbacks. All four are\n143\t+optional:\n144\t+\n145\t+```ts\n146\t+ctx.form({\n147\t+    reset () { /* form was reset */ },\n148\t+    disabled (isDisabled) { /* fieldset toggled */ },\n149\t+    restore (state, mode) { /* autocomplete / back-forward */ },\n150\t+    associated (form) { /* moved into or out of a form */ },\n151\t+})\n152\t+```\n153\t+\n154\t+Calling `ctx.form()` again replaces the earlier handlers. Handlers\n155\t+are dropped when the host tears down. A `restore` callback that fires\n156\t+before setup has registered a handler is replayed once the handler is\n157\t+set; `reset`, `disabled` and `associated` are not replayed because\n158\t+their state is readable at setup time (`host.matches(':disabled')`,\n159\t+`ctx.internals.form`).\n160\t+\n161\t+Components that do not call `.formAssociated()` behave exactly as\n162\t+before and do not appear in `FormData`.\n163\t+\n164\t+---------------------------------------------------------\n165\t \n166\t ### `builder.render(fn, options?)`\n167\t \n168\tdiff --git a/docs/adr/ADR-012-form-associated-components.md b/docs/adr/ADR-012-form-associated-components.md\n169\tnew file mode 100644\n170\tindex 0000000..754293c\n171\t--- /dev/null\n172\t+++ b/docs/adr/ADR-012-form-associated-components.md\n173\t@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@\n174\t+# ADR-012: Form-associated custom elements\n175\t+\n176\t+**Date:** 2026-11-24\n177\t+\n178\t+**Status:** Accepted\n179\t+\n180\t+**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size)\n181\t+\n182\t+## Context\n183\t+\n184\t+A component author who wants to build a form control (a custom input,\n185\t+a rich text field, a rating widget) cannot make it a real form control\n186\t+with microtags. The platform way is a form-associated custom element:\n187\t+the class sets a static `formAssociated = true`, each host gets an\n188\t+`ElementInternals` from `attachInternals()`, and the browser wires it\n189\t+into the containing form for submission, validation, and disabled\n190\t+state. Microtags calls `customElements.define` inside `setup()` with\n191\t+no way to set the static first, and does not expose\n192\t+`ElementInternals` to the setup callback.\n193\t+\n194\t+The first consumer is `markdown-area`, a `<textarea>` replacement.\n195\t+\n196\t+## Decision\n197\t+\n198\t+A new builder link, `.formAssociated()`, opts a component into the\n199\t+platform's form-associated custom element behaviour. It takes no\n200\t+arguments.\n201\t+\n202\t+- **Builder link.** `.formAssociated()` returns a new builder with an\n203\t+  internal `formAssociated` flag. The flag propagates through all\n204\t+  subsequent links. It composes with `withProps`, `withRefs`,\n205\t+  `withContexts` and `render` in any order.\n206\t+\n207\t+- **Static.** The factory sets `static formAssociated = true` on the\n208\t+  generated class before the builder calls `customElements.define`,\n209\t+  so the browser reads it at define time.\n210\t+\n211\t+- **Internals.** A form-associated host calls `attachInternals()`\n212\t+  once, in its constructor. The result is kept on the instance and\n213\t+  reused across disconnect/reconnect cycles. Setup receives it as\n214\t+  `ctx.internals`.\n215\t+\n216\t+- **Setup context.** For a form-associated component the setup context\n217\t+  gains `internals:ElementInternals`. Components that did not opt in\n218\t+  get a type error when they read `ctx.internals`.\n219\t+\n220\t+- **Form lifecycle callbacks.** The class installs\n221\t+  `formResetCallback`, `formDisabledCallback`,\n222\t+  `formStateRestoreCallback` and `formAssociatedCallback` on the\n223\t+  prototype. Each forwards to handlers registered through the\n224\t+  `ctx.form(handlers)` method. The `restore` callback is replayed\n225\t+  when a handler is registered; the others are not (their state is\n226\t+  readable from the host and `internals`). Calling `ctx.form()` again\n227\t+  replaces the earlier handlers. Handlers are dropped on teardown.\n228\t+\n229\t+- **Server render.** `render-support` is unchanged: form association\n230\t+  has no server-side meaning.\n231\t+\n232\t+- **Types.** `FormAssociatedContext` is a public type export from\n233\t+  `microtags`, so declaration emit in consuming packages does not hit\n234\t+  TS2883. The builder carries a `FormAssoc` type parameter that\n235\t+  controls whether the setup context includes `internals`.\n236\t+\n237\t+## Size cost\n238\t+\n239\t+| Entry | Before | After | Delta |\n240\t+|-------|--------|-------|-------|\n241\t+| `microtags` (core, ticket 02) | 4.04 kB | 4.09 kB | +50 B |\n242\t+| `microtags` (core, ticket 03) | 4.09 kB | 4.23 kB | +140 B |\n243\t+\n244\t+The ticket 02 delta (50 B) covers the `formAssociated` static, the\n245\t+`attachInternals()` call in the constructor, and passing internals to\n246\t+the setup context. The ticket 03 delta (140 B) adds four prototype\n247\t+callbacks, `ctx.form()` with handler storage, and restore replay.\n248\t+Both are under the 150 B-per-ticket target.\n249\t+\n250\t+## Consequences\n251\t+\n252\t+- Authors can build form controls that submit values, participate in\n253\t+  constraint validation, follow `disabled` from ancestor fieldsets,\n254\t+  and hear about form reset and state restore.\n255\t+- Components that do not opt in pay no runtime cost and no API change.\n256\t+- The core entry limit rises from 4.1 kB to 4.25 kB.\n257\t+\n258\t+[adr-004]: ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\n259\tdiff --git a/docs/adr/INDEX.md b/docs/adr/INDEX.md\n260\tindex 374a97c..6dcaf45 100644\n261\t--- a/docs/adr/INDEX.md\n262\t+++ b/docs/adr/INDEX.md\n263\t@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ consume these and `CONTEXT.md` for the project glossary.\n264\t | [ADR-009][adr-009] | Server render support loaded through the render link (amends ADR-005) | 2026-10-14 |\n265\t | [ADR-010][adr-010] | Preact owns the host, the element owns its children | 2026-11-08 |\n266\t | [ADR-011][adr-011] | Core renders an empty host with a kept render link (amends ADR-010) | 2026-11-10 |\n267\t+| [ADR-012][adr-012] | Form-associated custom elements | 2026-11-24 |\n268\t \n269\t [adr-006]: ADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md\n270\t [adr-007]: ADR-007-client-templater.md\n271\t@@ -24,3 +25,4 @@ consume these and `CONTEXT.md` for the project glossary.\n272\t [adr-009]: ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md\n273\t [adr-010]: ADR-010-preact-adapter-ownership-split.md\n274\t [adr-011]: ADR-011-core-renders-empty-host.md\n275\t+[adr-012]: ADR-012-form-associated-components.md\n276\tdiff --git a/src/builders.ts b/src/builders.ts\n277\tindex a9b1612..8a160d8 100644\n278\t--- a/src/builders.ts\n279\t+++ b/src/builders.ts\n280\t@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ import type {\n281\t     PropType,\n282\t     PropertyOnlyProp,\n283\t     SetupContext,\n284\t+    FormAssociatedContext,\n285\t     Coercer,\n286\t     RefDef,\n287\t     SingleRefDef,\n288\t@@ -204,46 +205,48 @@ export type MicrotagElementClass<\n289\t  * Fluent builder that accumulates props/refs/contexts config\n290\t  * before registering a custom element via `.setup()`.\n291\t  */\n292\t+interface BuilderConfig {\n